                <pb facs="0195" n="59" xml:id="pg59"/>

                <head>Informal suggestions for further implementing the Treaty for the Renunciation
                    of War, signed at Paris, August 27, 1928<anchor n="1" xml:id="ch2-f1"/></head>
                <p>[On July 25, 1929, during the discussions arising out of the Sino-Russian
                    controversy, the Secretary of State made a suggestion for the implementation of
                    the Kellogg-Briand Pact, i. e., the Treaty for the Renunciation of War; see
                    memorandum by the Secretary of State, “Suggestions for a Commission of
                    Conciliation,” <ref target="frus:frus1929v02/pg_243">volume II, page
                    243</ref>.]</p>




